/-
  Phys.Algebra.DerivationDblPhase — N186: THE U(1) HYPERCHARGE PHASE ALGEBRA
  `so(Born on Dbl ℚ) ≅ so(2) ≅ u(1)`, dimension 1 — the THIRD Standard-Model
  gauge factor's rank, on the complex-unit rung `Dbl ℚ`.
  ===========================================================================
  THE THIRD SM GAUGE FACTOR. The Standard-Model gauge group `SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1)`
  now has its COLOUR `SU(3) ⊂ G₂ = Der(O)` banked (N42a/b/c, `dim G₂ = 14`, N20) and
  its WEAK-ISOSPIN `SU(2) = Der(H)` banked (N184 bracket `⁅ad_i,ad_j⁆ = 2·ad_k` +
  N185 `dim = 3`). THIS node banks the remaining U(1) HYPERCHARGE factor — the abelian
  phase rotation on the cascade's FIRST doubling, the complex-unit rung `Dbl ℚ` (N2),
  one Cayley–Dickson step BELOW the quaternions `H ℚ = CD (Dbl ℚ)`.

  ★ THE KEY MEASUREMENT (docs/RUNBOOK.md W9 measure-first, frozen in PREREG). `Dbl ℚ` is
  COMMUTATIVE, so its INNER derivations VANISH (`ad_q = q·x − x·q = 0` for all `q`) — the
  U(1) is NOT an inner-derivation story like su(2)/g₂. The correct, theory-faithful object
  is the SKEW-ROTATION algebra of the self-overlap (Born) form: the skew-adjoint operators
  `so(bForm)` of `bForm v w := (v · star w).re` on the 2-dimensional `Dbl ℚ`. This is
  `so(2)`, and `so(2) ≅ u(1)` is the abelian 1-dimensional Lie algebra GENERATED by the
  phase rotation `z ↦ J·z` — exactly multiplication by the DERIVED complex unit `J`
  (the fold-root `mulJ_isFoldRoot`, N2), whose square is `−1`.

  ★ THE ROUTE — the so(n)-bound (N28) reused at the smallest rung (docs/RUNBOOK.md W2:
  import-and-USE a banked theorem). N28 (`DerivationIrreducibleFull.lean`) BUILT FORWARD
  the so(n)-type dimension bound `finrank_skewAdjoint_le_choose`: the skew-adjoint operators
  of a symmetric nondegenerate form on a `d`-dimensional space have dimension `≤ C(d, 2)`,
  via the exterior-power injection `D ↦ ((x,y) ↦ Φ (D x) y)` into `Dual (⋀² V)`. Applied to
  `V = Dbl ℚ` (`finrank = 2`, banked N19 `finrank_dbl_eq_two`): the UPPER bound is
  `C(2, 2) = 1`. The LOWER bound is the nonzero skew generator `L_J` (`L_J ≠ 0` and
  skew-adjoint), giving `1 ≤ dim`. Hence `dim = 1` — the dim-1 analog of `dim G₂ = 14`
  (colour) and `dim su(2) = 3` (isospin), here the FULL classification-sufficient signature
  (there is exactly ONE 1-dimensional Lie algebra up to isomorphism — necessarily abelian).

  WHAT IS BANKED HERE (forward, foundations-only):
    bForm              — the self-overlap (Born) form `(v,w) ↦ (v · star w).re` on `Dbl ℚ`.
    bForm_self         — `bForm v v = v.re² + v.im²` (the positivity, one rung down).
    bForm_isSymm       — `bForm` is symmetric.
    bForm_self_eq_zero — anisotropy: `bForm v v = 0 ↔ v = 0` (the Born positivity).
    bForm_nondegenerate— `bForm` is nondegenerate (definite ⟹ nondegenerate).
    L_J                — the phase rotation `z ↦ J·z` (multiplication by the complex unit).
    L_J_skew           — ★ the phase rotation is SKEW-ADJOINT for `bForm` (`J* = −J`).
    L_J_ne_zero        — the phase rotation is genuinely nonzero (W8 anti-vacuity).
    dim_le_one         — UPPER bound `dim so(bForm) ≤ C(2,2) = 1` (the so(n)-bound N28).
    skewAdjoint_ne_bot — the skew-adjoint algebra is nonzero (contains `L_J`).
    one_le_dim         — LOWER bound `1 ≤ dim so(bForm)`.
    finrank_phase_eq_one — ★★ THE u(1) ≅ so(2) DIMENSION = 1 (the third SM gauge rank).
    phase_eq_span_L_J  — ★ the WHOLE phase algebra IS the span of `L_J`: the derived complex
                         unit `J` GENERATES the entire u(1) (the generator is the algebra).

